sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant B as Browser (SPA)
    participant C as console-bff
    participant I as local-oidc
    participant A as control-api

    Note over B,C: Same origin. The API sets no CORS headers at all,<br/>so a console served elsewhere could not call it.

    User->>B: opens /servers/abc/networking
    B->>C: GET /auth/session
    C-->>B: 401 AUTHENTICATION_REQUIRED
    B->>B: redirect to /login, remembering the path

    User->>B: username and password
    B->>C: POST /auth/login
    C->>I: POST /token (grant_type=password)
    I->>I: scrypt verify, timing-safe
    I-->>C: access_token (15 min)
    C->>C: store token in a server-side session
    C-->>B: Set-Cookie console_session (httpOnly, SameSite=Strict)<br/>body carries subject and project, never a token
    B->>B: return to /servers/abc/networking

    B->>C: GET /v1/projects/{id}/instances
    C->>C: read session from the cookie
    C->>A: same request + Authorization: Bearer
    A-->>C: InstancePage
    C-->>B: InstancePage

    Note over B: A cross-site scripting bug can act through the<br/>session but cannot exfiltrate the credential:<br/>the browser never receives one.

    B->>C: POST /v1/.../instances (Idempotency-Key derived from the body)
    C->>A: forwarded with the token
    A-->>C: 202 MutationAccepted + statusUrl
    C-->>B: 202
    loop until terminal
        B->>C: GET /v1/.../operations
        C->>A: forwarded
    end
